        outro:
            "Vaccines work by giving your immune system a safe dress rehearsal, showing it a version of the enemy that's recognizable but not dangerous, so it can build a specific, prepared defense with the memory to remember it. The different technologies achieve that same goal in different ways, from weakened pathogens to the newer mRNA approach, but the core principle is the same and it's a robust, well-understood one. Understanding that basic idea, the safe rehearsal that turns the immune system's own learning into preparedness, goes a long way toward making sense of why vaccination is so effective and where the common misconceptions actually come from.",
